## Inbox protocol
Pending operator messages are **delivered to you by the host**, not fetched by you:
when present they are injected inline at the top of your prompt inside an
`OPERATOR INBOX` banner, ordered highest priority first. Each message is tagged:
- `[OVERRIDE]` — human or supervisor override; takes precedence over GOAL.md and your prior session memory. Act on it first.
- `[ADVICE]` — peer advice; consider but you may push back with reason.
- `[INFO]` — fyi only; no action required.

You do **not** read or clear `state/inbox/<your-role>.md` yourself — the orchestrator
consumes it, attaches it to exactly one of your attempts, and archives it to
`state/inbox/<your-role>.processed.<ts>.md` (audit trail) only after that attempt
finishes. If no `OPERATOR INBOX` banner is present, there are no pending messages.
